            0.148,
            0.142,
            0.264,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": "**Figure it out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.17,
            0.882,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": "**Q.1. Find the prime factorisations of the following numbers: 64, 104, 105, 243, 320, 141, 1728, 729, 1024, 1331, 1000.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.213,
            0.539,
            0.506
          ],
          "sub_type": "code",
          "content": "```txt\nAns. 64 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2\n104 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 13\n105 = 3 × 5 × 7\n243 = 3 ×3 ×3 ×3 ×3\n320 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 5\n141 = 3 × 47\n1728 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 3 × 3 × 3\n729 = 3 ×3 ×3 × 3 ×3 ×3\n1024 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 ×2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2\n1331 = 11 × 11 × 11\n1000 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 5 × 5 × 5\n```",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.514,
            0.881,
            0.549
          ],
          "content": "**Q.2. The prime factorisation of a number has one 2, two 3s, and one 11. What is the number?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.559,
            0.334,
            0.576
          ],
          "sub_type": "code",
          "content": "```txt\nAns. 198 = 2 × 3 × 3 × 11\n```",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.586,
            0.734,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "**Q.3. Find three prime numbers, all less than 30, whose product is 1955.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.614,
            0.323,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** 1955 = 5 × 17 × 23"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.64,
            0.776,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": "**Q.4. Find the prime factorisation of these numbers without multiplying first**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.667,
            0.533,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{a}.56 \\times 25 \\quad \\mathrm{b}.108 \\times 75 \\quad \\mathrm{c}.1000 \\times 81",
          "image_source": "images/page_28_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.696,
            0.163,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.831,
            0.68,
            0.849
          ],
          "content": "**Q.5. What is the smallest number whose prime factorisation has:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.858,
            0.466,
            0.876
          ],
          "content": "**a. three different prime numbers?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.885,
            0.458,
            0.903
          ],
          "content": "**b. four different prime numbers?**"
